Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||03-27-2001||02:14 PM||||That reminds me of a story I read in the newspaper about 6 years ago (I read this in Holland's largest newspaper).<P>They we're interviewing a guy in a hospital in Spain. The guy had third degree burn wounds on his buttocks and a broken leg. This was his story:<P>Apparantly, his wife had caught a cockroach earlier that day. She didn't want to kill it the ol' fashioned way (rolled-up newspaper) because of the mess that would make. So she caught it in a jar and brought it to the bathroom. She threw it in the toilet but no matter how often she tried to flush it, the cockroach would surface and try to climb out. So she got the bug-spray and almost emptied the spray-can in the toilet until the cockroach was finally dead. This of course did not help trying to flush the cockroach so eventually, she took it out and simply threw the dead cockroach away. Later that afternoon her husband returned home and he needed to use the bathroom for "a big one". It was his habit to smoke while he was sitting on the toilet. When he was almost done with his sigarette, he threw it between his legs into the pot. Apparantly, the pot was still filled with gas (which was heavier than air) from the spray-can and her over-active spraying had also left some highy flammable agent. Needless to say the toilet exploded between his legs.<P>This explained how he got the burns but it didn't explain his broken leg. When the interviewer asked about his broken leg, he answered that he had told his story to the paramedics while they were carrying him on a sretcher down the stairs. They laughed so hard they accidently dropped him...<BR>||||reg||6
