Z||000008||FieroLisa||03-27-2001||09:24 PM||||Here's another one: In England, or somewhere there over seas, there was a newspaper article (and I've read it in its original version, so its true)<P>A guy was walking around when 2 kids drove by throwing fruit and vegetables at people. One kid through a turnip at this guy walking. It hit him in the back of the head. Because of the speed the kids were driving, the turnip had that speed as well as the speed it was thrown at. Hitting the other guy in the back of the head was enough to kill him. Ouch, death by turnip.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||03-27-2001||11:08 PM||||Okay. More stupid human tricks...<BR>My cousin told me this story.<BR>This happened sometime in the 60s, somewhere around Philadelphia. <BR>Seems that he and some of his friends were riding around, just raising hell, pounding on the car doors and hollering at people. Especially women. <BR>One of his *brilliant* friends decided that it would be a neat thing to swat this girl on the a$$ as they drove past at what seemed like a reasonable speed. Like 25 or so.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>To make a long story short, it knocked the girl flat on her back on the sidewalk, and drove his arm back into the doorpost, breaking it (the arm, not the doorpost) in two places.<BR>DOH!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000010||Hank is Here||03-28-2001||03:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><BR>The deceased male was dressed in a full wet suit, complete with SCUBA tanks on his back, flippers, and face mask. <BR>A post-mortem revealed that the person died not from burns, but from massive internal injuries.<BR>Dental records provided a positive identification. <BR>Investigators then set about to determine how a fully clad diver ended up in the middle of a forest fire..<BR>It was revealed that, on the day of the fire, the person went for a diving trip off the coast some 20 miles away from the forest..<BR>The firefighters, seeking to control the fire as quickly as possible, called in a fleet of helicopters with very large dip buckets.  Water was dipped from the ocean then flown to the forest fire and emptied..<BR>You guessed it. One minute our diver was making like Flipper in the Pacific, the next he was doing the breast stroke in a fire dip bucket 300 feet in the air. Apparently he extinguished exactly 5'-10" of the fire..<BR>Some days it just doesn't pay to get out of bed!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was thinknig about this last night.  I know nothing about scuba or chemistry but wouldn't having a tank of compressed O2 on the divers back basically be a bomb waiting to explode in the fire?  Then basically fter the explosion there would be nothing left.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||loafer87gt||03-28-2001||04:04 PM||||Gawd, the poor bastard. Reminds me of another story I heard about a guy up North who was hosting a big get together at his house. Apparently he was a fairly connected individual, and pursuaded oneof the local water bomber pilots to dump a load of water on his acreage. He was shocked to find that instead of getting a nice rainstorm misty effect like he had planned, the force of the water totally destroyed his house. Dumbass. I can only imagine the pilot lost his job over the deal as well.||||reg||10
